." ECMVS Project Guide
.TH ECMVS 7 "August 2026" "ECMVS" "Project Guide"
.SH ECMVS PROJECT GUIDE
.B ECMVS
is an Enterprise Compliance & Vendor Management System. It records concerns, assigns owners, investigates facts, assesses risk, manages corrective actions, sends notifications, and preserves an audit trail.
.SH WHAT IS INCLUDED
.IP \(bu 2
Compliance Hub for Grievance, Fraud, Health & Safety, Conflict of Interest, Vendor Risk, and Employee compliance.
.IP \(bu 2
Vendor issue management with assignment, comments, priority, status, due dates, and search.
.IP \(bu 2
Investigations with findings, root cause, evidence, notes, and officer scoping.
.IP \(bu 2
Risk assessment using Likelihood multiplied by Impact.
.IP \(bu 2
Resolution workflow with corrective action, preventive action, approval, rejection, and closure.
.IP \(bu 2
JWT login, role permissions, dashboards, notifications, reports, user administration, and audit logs.
.IP \(bu 2
Responsive desktop and mobile interface with the existing ECMVS logo preserved.
.SH COMPLIANCE DOMAINS
.TP
.B Grievance
Workplace concerns, speak-up reports, confidentiality, and anonymous reporting.
.TP
.B Fraud
Suspected dishonest activity, financial allegations, and forensic investigation intake.
.TP
.B Health & Safety
Incidents, hazards, injuries, near misses, location, and corrective action.
.TP
.B Conflict of Interest
Disclosures, related parties, recusals, and ethical review.
.TP
.B Vendor Risk
Third-party exposure, due diligence, owners, severity, and remediation tracking.
.TP
.B Employee
Employee compliance, conduct, and ethics attestation matters.
.SH BASIC WORKFLOW
.IP 1. 3
Open Compliance Hub and select New case.
.IP 2. 3
Choose the domain and severity.
.IP 3. 3
Enter the facts, subject, location, confidentiality, and anonymous reporter setting.
.IP 4. 3
Create, search, filter, assign, investigate, act, and close the case.
.PP
Vendor issues follow: create, assign, investigate, assess risk, create resolution, approve, resolve, close, and review audit history.
.SH ROLES
.TP
.B Super Administrator
Full administration, users, audit, and all workflows.
.TP
.B Compliance Officer
Investigations, risk assessments, and resolutions.
.TP
.B Vendor Manager
Vendor issues, assignment, and vendor operations.
.TP
.B Approver
Reviews and approves or rejects resolutions.
.TP
.B Employee
Reports concerns and views permitted information.
.SH TECHNOLOGY
React 18, TypeScript, Vite, React Router, Axios, and Recharts are used for the frontend. ASP.NET Core 8 and C# provide the API. MongoDB stores data through MongoDB.Driver. JWT provides authentication and Swagger provides API documentation.
.SH PROJECT FOLDERS
.IP \(bu 2
frontend/src/pages: screens.
.IP \(bu 2
frontend/src/components: shared UI.
.IP \(bu 2
frontend/src/services: API clients.
.IP \(bu 2
backend/Controllers: endpoints.
.IP \(bu 2
backend/Services: business logic.
.IP \(bu 2
backend/Models and DTOs: data contracts.
.IP \(bu 2
database/seed.js: demo data and indexes.
.SH LOCAL STARTUP
.nf
Docker MongoDB:
docker run -d --name ecmvs-mongodb -p 27017:27017 mongo:7
docker cp database/seed.js ecmvs-mongodb:/tmp/seed.js
docker exec ecmvs-mongodb mongosh --quiet /tmp/seed.js

Backend:
cd backend
dotnet restore
dotnet run --urls http://localhost:5128

Frontend:
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
.fi
.PP
Open http://localhost:5173. API: http://localhost:5128. Swagger: http://localhost:5128/swagger.
